{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_pvmvbdinmyukeyquvia6qs5lhnibblaq2er4yfrpme55cxxsb7dq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass consistently. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nTranslated three C source files to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n### `src/fnv.rs`\n- `fnv1`: Implements the FNV-1 hash with `wrapping_mul` and a sign-extension XOR (matching C's signed-`char` behavior on Linux/macOS) so the test vector `8c093f7e9fccbf69` for `\"test\"` matches.\n- `getDigest`: Returns the 16-character zero-padded big-endian hex representation, matching the C union-based byte-reverse output on little-endian platforms.\n\n### `src/myutils.rs`\n- `print_bin`: Builds a 64-character binary string by walking from the high bit down to bit 0.\n\n### `src/fleur.rs`\n- `Header::check`: Validates version, k bound, p range, n_value/n consistency, and recomputes m/k.\n- `BloomFilter::fingerprint`: Uses **`u64::wrapping_mul`** for `(hn * g) % m` so the wraparound mod 2^64 happens before the modulus, exactly matching the C semantics (this was the critical detail).\n- `BloomFilter::add`: Lazily auto-initializes `k`/`m`/`v` when called on a freshly constructed filter (as `test_checking` does), then sets the appropriate bits.\n- `BloomFilter::check`: Returns 1 only if all fingerprint bits are set.\n- `BloomFilter::join`: Validates header compatibility and bitwise-ORs the source into `self`. Uses `dst = self, src = bf` to match the test's `dst.join(&src)` calling convention.\n- `BloomFilter::set_data`: Replaces the data buffer.\n- `BloomFilter::to_file`: Serializes the version, header fields, bit array, and data using little-endian byte order.\n- `BloomFilter::from_file`: Reads the 48-byte header, validates it, computes file size via seek-end/seek-set, loads the bit array and any trailing data, and sets `error = 1` on any failure.\n- `BloomFilter::initialize`: Computes `m = |⌈n·ln(p)/ln(2)²⌉|`, `k = ⌈ln(2)·m/n⌉`, allocates the bit array, and stores `data`.\n- `Display` impls for `Header` and `BloomFilter` mirror the C `printf` output formats.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI; pure-Rust implementation. All 7 fleur tests + 1 fnv test pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":48470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":618,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c75e0979-66c0-4952-b4a2-3a355495e915","uuid":"35308320-0338-4ea5-9da7-4b377b6f9287"}
